# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS committed (this workspace produces binaries).

# --- Blizzard-owned content: NEVER commit ---
# The user's legally-installed 1.12.1 client. Read at runtime; not redistributed.
/WoW
# The user's legally-installed Classic Era client (product wow_classic_era; the shared CASC Data
# dir sits beside the product dir). Source of the Era UI exports for decision 0068; not redistributed.
/WoW-era
# Cached / extracted assets derived from the user's install.
/extracted/
/out/
# Real client files used as test fixtures (document expected paths, do not commit).
**/tests/fixtures/

# --- benilla's own local state (decision 0954, moved out of the install by 1175) ---
# The one folder benilla persists into: config.toml, macros/, bindings/, saved-variables.lua,
# camera/. A dev build resolves it to the primary checkout (so the worktree pool shares one); a
# release build puts it beside the binary — which is why it is not called `benilla/`: that name
# collides with the binary of the same name. Machine-local by definition — `crate::local_state`
# is the only thing in the tree that may write it.
/benilla-config

# Worktree-pool claim marker (scripts/wt.sh) — per-slot state, never content.
/.wt-claimed

# Profiling output: `--features bevy/trace_chrome` drops a multi-GB flame chart in the cwd, which
# otherwise leaves the checkout "dirty" and blocks the worktree verbs (decision 0610).
trace-*.json

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
/.idea/
# Claude Code: share the project hooks + settings + slash commands + skills, ignore per-machine state.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/hooks/
!/.claude/commands/
!/.claude/skills/
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Python bytecode from the `scripts/` tooling.
__pycache__/

# The vanilla addon corpus the UI engine's real-addon tests read (third-party content, decision
# 2329): a symlink `scripts/wt.sh` lays into every slot and the primary, beside `WoW`.
/wow-addons-vanilla
